    "title": {
     "en": "Animal jumps"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "The frog jumps 3 steps at a time. Which numbers will it touch? A squirrel jumps 4 steps, a rabbit 6 steps and a kangaroo 8."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "multiple",
     "jump",
     "skip count",
     "times"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "The frog jumps 3 steps at a time and touches 3, 6, 9, 12 and so on. These numbers are multiples of 3.\nThe squirrel jumps 4 at a time: 4, 8, 12 and more. How many jumps to reach 60? 60 ÷ 4 = 15 jumps.\nThe rabbit jumps 6 at a time and the kangaroo 8 at a time. Are there numbers that both touch? Yes, like 24 and 48.\nTo reach 48 the rabbit needs 8 jumps and the kangaroo needs 6 jumps.\nMultiplication and division are linked: 6 × 8 = 48 and 48 ÷ 6 = 8."
    }
   },
